    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d223">

                <pb facs="0252" n="248" xml:id="pg248"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/15372: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-13T19:00:00+01:00">September 13,
                            1939—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 13—6:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1953. For Hornbeck. Your 884, September 12, 5 p.m.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d223-f1"
                    /> I have not transmitted and will not transmit the message you communicated in
                    your telegram under reference. I have, however, requested Rajchman’s eminent
                    associate in Paris to inform Rajchman that I resent his attempt to use me as a
                    hopper for communications of this sort.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d223-f1" n="29" xml:id="d223-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see telegram No. 170, September 12, 5 p.m., to the Ambassador in
                    China, <ref target="#pg245">p. 245</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
